  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "For a long while now, if a user wanted to implement realistic locomotion animations for laying down on your back/side or wanted to talk to users whilst sitting down in a chair in a cramped room, there was no option to choose 3 point tracking idle states for crouching and prone animations. They'd have to implement realistic \"laying down\" animations, whether it be legs crisscrossed, or on your back, in the Unity editor manually.\n\nThe crouching and prone animations make Quest users appear to \"float\" with their legs above the ground or in-prone idle states look as if they're doing \"handless push-ups\" with an uncomfortable bend in the back. Allowing for a set of idle and prone animations to be selected during runtime in the options radial menu would remove the discomfort of VRChat whilst sitting down. Since avatar locomotion is mostly universal, having customizability for how your avatar sits/crouches/lays down would better fit the 3 point tracking bound Quest users, along with people who are new to VR.",
